<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Privacy Policy · Learn with me</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css"><%- include('partials/adsense-verification') %></head>
<body>
<header class="topbar"><a class="brand" href="/">Learn with me</a></header>
<main class="container">
  <div class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: August 28, 2026</p>

    <p>Learn with me is a private developer tool that provides a searchable library of Guidewire Gosu query files to authorized users, with more topics planned. This Privacy Policy explains what information the application may collect, how it is used, and the choices available to you.</p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>By using the application you do not need to provide any personal information directly. When you sign in with Google, Google shares the basic account profile information required for authentication, which may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your Google account identifier used to recognize you as a returning user.</li>
      <li>Your email address.</li>
      <li>Your display name.</li>
      <li>Basic Google account/profile details required to complete sign-in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>In addition, while you use the application, limited usage information is recorded so that the library can be understood and improved. For example, when you view or copy a query, the application records which query was used and when.</p>
    <p>The application does not collect your Google password or other credentials, payment information, or sensitive personal data.</p>

    <h2>How Your Information Is Used</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Authentication: verifying your identity when you sign in with Google.</li>
      <li>Account identification: recognizing you as a returning user and maintaining your account record.</li>
      <li>Access control: tracking your access period and enforcing expiration and authorization rules.</li>
      <li>Providing the application: displaying the library, search, and query pages you are authorized to see.</li>
      <li>Usage understanding: summarizing which queries are viewed or copied so the library can be improved.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sign-in with Google</h2>
    <p>Learn with me uses Google Sign-In, which works through the OAuth 2.0 protocol. When you choose to sign in with Google, Google asks you to approve the information shared with the application, which typically includes your name, email address, and basic Google account/profile information needed for authentication.</p>
    <p>The application never receives or stores your Google password. You can review, manage, or revoke the application's access to your Google account at any time from your Google Account settings.</p>

    <h2>Data Retention and Security</h2>
    <p>Your account record includes the Google account identifier, email address, display name, sign-in times, and access expiration date. This information is stored in our database for as long as it is needed to provide and administer your access to the application.</p>
    <p>Usage records are retained to support the operation of the library. We do not sell your personal information, and it is not shared with third parties except as required by applicable law.</p>
    <p>We apply reasonable security safeguards, including secure session handling and restricted database access. Access to the library expires after the configured access period, and the library administrator can renew or revoke access at any time.</p>

    <h2>Account Inactivity and Automatic Deletion</h2>
    <p>Accounts may be automatically deleted after 60 consecutive days of inactivity. We use account activity, including authenticated activity, to determine whether an account has remained inactive for 60 consecutive days.</p>
    <p>Only accounts whose status is not active are eligible for automatic deletion. Active accounts are never automatically deleted. Accounts with the Owner or Administrator role and any email addresses configured as administrator contacts are excluded from automatic deletion.</p>
    <p>When an eligible account is deleted, the deletion is permanent and cannot be undone. The account would need to be created again and re-authorized to use the application.</p>
    <p>When an account is automatically deleted, the following categories of data associated with that account may be permanently removed, to the extent they exist: account profile information; session records; content interactions such as likes, private learner notes, and discussions and replies; viewing history such as recently viewed and content seen records; usage records such as query views and video views; premium and entitlement records related to products, plans, orders and subscriptions; and related audit log entries. Only data actually stored for the account is removed; no additional retention periods are implied.</p>

    <h2>Premium and Protected Content</h2>
    <p>Premium and protected content made available through the application is intended for your authorized personal use only.</p>
    <p>The website may use technical measures intended to discourage unauthorized copying, recording, downloading, or redistribution of premium and protected content. These measures cannot guarantee that screen recording or other forms of copying are technically impossible, and the application does not use DRM.</p>
    <p>We do not claim to detect or completely prevent every instance of screen recording or copying.</p>

    <h2>Your Choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You can sign out of the application at any time.</li>
      <li>You can manage or remove the application's access to your Google account from your Google Account settings.</li>
      <li>You can contact the library administrator to ask questions about your data or to request that your account be removed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or about the information collected by the application, please contact the library administrator who granted you access.</p>
  </div>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body></html>